# Newsletter Management Rules

Newsletter templates use MJML for email-compatible HTML generation.
Newsletters are created from content and sent via Mailchimp.
Templates must be responsive and follow email best practices.

<RULES>
1. Use MJML syntax for email template structure
2. Follow Mailchimp merge tag conventions
3. Ensure mobile responsiveness
4. Include required sections: header, content, footer
5. Use proper image handling for email clients
6. Include unsubscribe links and legal requirements
7. Test across multiple email clients
</RULES>

<EXAMPLES>
```mjml
<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-title>Newsletter Title</mj-title>
    <mj-preview>Preview text</mj-preview>
  </mj-head>
  <mj-body>
    <mj-section>
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text>
          Content with *|MERGE|* tags
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
```
</EXAMPLES>

<VALIDATION>
- Verify MJML syntax
- Check Mailchimp merge tags
- Test responsive layout
- Validate email client compatibility
- Ensure all required sections are present
</VALIDATION>